#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
fake-claude: a stand-in for the `claude` CLI that speaks the same stream-json protocol with canned
behaviour. Point FACTORY_CLAUDE_BIN at it to develop the UI or run end-to-end tests without spending
tokens. It understands the flags Agern passes (-p, --output-format stream-json, --input-format
stream-json, --resume, --json-schema, --append-system-prompt, --mcp-config, --model, ...).

Behaviour
  Chat (--input-format stream-json): every user message gets a streamed reply "You said: <text>".
    - text containing "slow"  -> streams ~10 s of output (try interrupting it)
    - text containing "tool"  -> also emits a Bash tool_use + tool_result
    - text containing "mcp"   -> calls the factory MCP endpoint (initialize + tools/list) with the
                                 bearer token from --mcp-config and lists the tools it sees
    - text containing "crash" -> exits with status 3
    - text containing "env"   -> replies with the names of its environment variables
    - text containing "install" -> files a software request through the MCP tool factory_request_software
    - text containing "long"  -> replies with 80 numbered lines (a transcript taller than the screen)
    - text containing "fake:think" -> before the reply, "thinks" for ~3 s: 15 system/thinking_tokens progress events
                                 (estimated_tokens 100, 200, ... 1500), one every 0.2 s, like newer CLIs
    - text containing "fake:heartbeat" -> before the reply, runs a Bash tool call ("sleep 4") for ~4 s, sending a
                                 tool_progress heartbeat (elapsed_time_seconds 0, 0, 1, ... 3) every 0.5 s while it runs
    - "forward <runId> <role>: <message>" -> passes <message> to that run's agent through the MCP tool
                                 factory_send_to_agent and reports the tool's answer
    - "file issue: <title>" -> creates a bug issue with that title through the MCP tool
                                 factory_create_issue and reports the tool's answer
    - content blocks: image blocks are decoded and reported ("IMAGE 1: image/png 32x32, 70 bytes"); the
      "[Attachments]" text block's paths are checked on disk ("FILE ok name 123 bytes" / "FILE missing ...").
      Trigger words are only looked for in the user's own text, not in that listing.
    - control_request {subtype: interrupt} stops the current turn
    - only with an OAuth token (CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN), one rate_limit_event (the shape of the CLI 2.1.328 schema,
      utilization a fraction, resetsAt epoch seconds in the future) is emitted before the reply when the text contains:
        "usage-ok"    -> unifiedWindows five_hour 0.42 and seven_day 0.18, both "allowed"
        "usage-high"  -> unifiedWindows five_hour 0.86 "allowed_warning" and seven_day 0.18 "allowed"
        "usage-limit" -> top-level status "rejected", rateLimitType "five_hour", utilization 1.0, resetsAt now + 2 h
  Advisor (interactive, "# Role: advisor"): the agent a run's owner talks to at needs human, using the chat loop.
    Every message is answered "Advisor: <the owner's text>", followed by the "Needs a human because:" line and the
    reviewer headings ("### ...") found in the <run_context> block the server sent to this process, and the output
    of `git diff --stat <baseRef>...HEAD` (baseRef taken from the context).
    - text containing "please change" -> appends a line to AGERN_FAKE.md and commits it (the server then pushes and
                                 reviews it again)
    - "slow" and "crash" behave as in chat
  Conversations are remembered under $HOME/.fake-claude/sessions/<id>. Like the real CLI,
  --resume <id> of an unknown conversation fails at once ("No conversation found with session ID").
  A Claude credential containing "invalid" is rejected like a bad key ("Invalid API key").
  Pipeline stages, role taken from "# Role: <role>" in --append-system-prompt. Reviewers and the approver
  are one-shot (prompt on stdin as text). With --input-format stream-json (spec-writer, builder) the prompt
  is the first stream-json user message and stdin stays open; this mirrors the real CLI (verified with
  Claude Code 2.1.328, see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §6): a message written mid-turn is picked up after the
  current tool round of the same turn (with --replay-user-messages it is echoed back with "isReplay": true
  at that moment), and one that arrives after the last tool round starts a further turn with its own
  `result`. The process exits when stdin is closed.
    - spec-writer: prints a small spec
    - builder: appends a line to AGERN_FAKE.md and commits it (if the cwd is a git repository)
    - reviewers (--json-schema with PASS/CHANGES): PASS, unless the prompt contains
        "fake:changes" (CHANGES before the first fix round) or "fake:always-changes"
    - approver (--json-schema with APPROVE/ESCALATE): APPROVE, unless "fake:escalate"
    - "fake:fail-<role>" anywhere in the prompt makes that role exit with status 1 and no result
    - "fake:hang-<role>" makes that role hang until it is killed (stage time limit, cancel)
    - "fake:stop-builder" makes the builder commit and then stop with "API Error: Can't reach the API server", unless
        the prompt is a continuation ("Do not redo that work"), which builds normally
    - "fake:slow" makes every stage take ~1.5 s, so the pipeline can be watched advancing
    - "fake:markdown" makes reviewers and the approver write their summaries and findings in Markdown
      (lists, bold, inline code with a long path, a code block, a link and literal HTML)
    - "fake:sandbox" makes the builder call the MCP tools factory_sandbox_info and factory_sandbox_exec (command
        "echo built in the sandbox && ls") like a real agent (tool_use + tool_result events) and report both answers
        in its result ("Sandbox info: ..." / "Sandbox exec: ..."); with "fake:platform=<name>" it then runs the same
        command once more with that platform ("Sandbox exec on <name>: ...")
    - "fake:sandbox-long" makes the builder run one foreground factory_sandbox_exec ("sleep long"; a test makes it outlast
        the 10 s read timeout of mcp_call, so the answer has to come as a stream) and report it ("Sandbox exec: ...")
    - "fake:sandbox-background" makes the builder start "sleep long" with factory_sandbox_exec {background: true}, then
        call factory_sandbox_wait with the handle, and report both ("Sandbox start: ..." / "Sandbox wait: ...")
    - "fake:screenshots" makes the ux and ui-design reviewers, before answering, write a small PNG into their working
        directory, attach it through the MCP tool factory_attach_screenshot with the caption
        "Fake <role> screenshot (<build | fix round N>)", delete the file and append "Attached 1 screenshot." (or the
        tool's error text) to their summary; other roles ignore it
    - "fake:ui-change" makes the builder also write and commit web/src/FakeBanner.tsx, so the run's diff touches a UI
        file (without "fake:screenshots" Agern then warns "UI change reviewed without screenshots")
    - "fake:image" (optionally "fake:image=<n>") in a chat message calls the MCP tool factory_generate_image with the
        purpose "app icon" (and "issueNumber" from a "#<n>" in the message) and appends "Image tool: <answer>" to the reply;
        in a builder's prompt the builder calls it too, copies the first returned path to assets/fake-icon.png, commits
        it with its usual commit and appends "Image tool: <answer>" to its result
    - a spec-writer or builder whose prompt has an <images> block appends "PREPARED ok <path> <bytes>" or
        "PREPARED missing <path>" per listed "path:" line
    - "fake:busy-<role>" makes that (stream-json) role work in Bash steps of ~0.4 s for up to ~2 minutes,
      until a message from the owner contains "finish"; each picked-up message is acknowledged with
      "Noted the owner's message: ..." and listed in the final result
"""
import json
import os
import queue
import re
import shutil
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time
import urllib.request
import uuid
import zlib

args = sys.argv[1:]


def opt(name):
    if name in args:
        i = args.index(name)
        if i + 1 < len(args):
            return args[i + 1]
    return None


interactive = opt("--input-format") == "stream-json"
resume = opt("--resume")
schema = opt("--json-schema")
system_prompt = opt("--append-system-prompt") or ""
model = opt("--model") or "fake-model"
mcp_config = opt("--mcp-config")
session_id = resume or str(uuid.uuid4())
role = "chat"
for line in system_prompt.splitlines():
    if line.startswith("# Role:"):
        role = line.split(":", 1)[1].strip()
        break

out_lock = threading.Lock()
total_cost = 0.0


def emit(obj):
    with out_lock:
        sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(obj) + "\n")
        sys.stdout.flush()


SESSIONS_DIR = os.path.join(os.environ.get("HOME", "."), ".fake-claude", "sessions")


def remember_session():
    try:
        os.makedirs(SESSIONS_DIR, exist_ok=True)
        open(os.path.join(SESSIONS_DIR, session_id), "w").close()
    except OSError:
        pass


def init_event():
    remember_session()
    emit({"type": "system", "subtype": "init", "cwd": os.getcwd(), "session_id": session_id, "model": model,
          "tools": ["Bash", "Read", "Edit", "Write"], "mcp_servers": [{"name": "factory", "status": "connected"}],
          "permissionMode": "bypassPermissions", "apiKeySource": "none", "claude_code_version": "fake",
          "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})


def msg_id():
    return "msg_fake_" + uuid.uuid4().hex[:16]


def stream_text(text, chunk_delay=0.0, chunks=None, interrupted=lambda: False):
    """Streams text as stream_event deltas, then the complete assistant message. Returns False if interrupted."""
    mid = msg_id()
    emit({"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "message_start", "message": {"id": mid, "role": "assistant", "model": model, "content": []}},
          "session_id": session_id, "parent_tool_use_id": None, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
    emit({"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 0, "content_block": {"type": "text", "text": ""}},
          "session_id": session_id, "parent_tool_use_id": None, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
    parts = chunks or [text[i:i + 12] for i in range(0, len(text), 12)]
    sent = ""
    for p in parts:
        if interrupted():
            return False, sent
        emit({"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": p}},
              "session_id": session_id, "parent_tool_use_id": None, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
        sent += p
        if chunk_delay:
            time.sleep(chunk_delay)
    emit({"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 0}, "session_id": session_id,
          "parent_tool_use_id": None, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
    emit({"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": mid, "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "model": model,
                                           "content": [{"type": "text", "text": text}], "stop_reason": None,
                                           "usage": {"input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": len(text) // 4}},
          "parent_tool_use_id": None, "session_id": session_id, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
    return True, sent


def think(events=15, delay=0.2):
    """Progress of a model that thinks: system/thinking_tokens about every 100 tokens (newer CLIs, no content)."""
    for i in range(1, events + 1):
        emit({"type": "system", "subtype": "thinking_tokens", "estimated_tokens": 100 * i, "estimated_tokens_delta": 100,
              "session_id": session_id, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
        time.sleep(delay)


def heartbeat_tool(seconds=4.0, every=0.5):
    """A long tool call: tool_progress heartbeats while it runs (the CLI sends one every few seconds), then its result."""
    tid = "toolu_fake_" + uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]
    command = "sleep %d" % seconds
    emit({"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": msg_id(), "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "model": model,
                                           "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": tid, "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": command, "description": "Wait"}}]},
          "parent_tool_use_id": None, "session_id": session_id, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
    start = time.time()
    while time.time() - start < seconds:
        emit({"type": "tool_progress", "tool_use_id": tid, "tool_name": "Bash", "parent_tool_use_id": None,
              "elapsed_time_seconds": int(time.time() - start), "heartbeat": True,
              "session_id": session_id, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
        time.sleep(every)
    emit({"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": tid, "type": "tool_result", "content": "waited"}]},
          "parent_tool_use_id": None, "session_id": session_id, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})


def tool_roundtrip(command):
    tid = "toolu_fake_" + uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]
    emit({"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": msg_id(), "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "model": model,
                                           "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": tid, "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": command, "description": "Run " + command}}]},
          "parent_tool_use_id": None, "session_id": session_id, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
    try:
        output = subprocess.run(command, shell=True, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10).stdout[:2000]
    except Exception as e:  # noqa
        output = str(e)
    emit({"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": tid, "type": "tool_result", "content": output}]},
          "parent_tool_use_id": None, "session_id": session_id, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})


def result(text, subtype="success", is_error=False, structured=None, turns=1, cost=0.0123):
    global total_cost
    total_cost += cost
    r = {"type": "result", "subtype": subtype, "is_error": is_error, "duration_ms": 50, "duration_api_ms": 40,
         "num_turns": turns, "result": text, "stop_reason": "end_turn" if not is_error else None,
         "session_id": session_id, "total_cost_usd": round(total_cost, 6),
         "usage": {"input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 20}, "permission_denials": [], "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())}
    if structured is not None:
        r["structured_output"] = structured
    emit(r)


def rate_limit_event(content):
    """Emits a rate_limit_event for the usage-* trigger words in [content] (OAuth token only, like the real CLI)."""
    if not os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN"):
        return
    now = int(time.time())
    if "usage-limit" in content:
        info = {"status": "rejected", "rateLimitType": "five_hour", "utilization": 1.0, "resetsAt": now + 2 * 3600}
    elif "usage-high" in content:
        info = {"status": "allowed_warning", "rateLimitType": "five_hour", "utilization": 0.86, "resetsAt": now + 3 * 3600,
                "unifiedWindows": {
                    "five_hour": {"utilization": 0.86, "resetsAt": now + 3 * 3600, "status": "allowed_warning"},
                    "seven_day": {"utilization": 0.18, "resetsAt": now + 4 * 86400, "status": "allowed"}}}
    elif "usage-ok" in content:
        info = {"status": "allowed", "rateLimitType": "five_hour", "utilization": 0.42, "resetsAt": now + 2 * 3600 + 300,
                "unifiedWindows": {
                    "five_hour": {"utilization": 0.42, "resetsAt": now + 2 * 3600 + 300, "status": "allowed"},
                    "seven_day": {"utilization": 0.18, "resetsAt": now + 4 * 86400, "status": "allowed"}}}
    else:
        return
    emit({"type": "rate_limit_event", "rate_limit_info": info, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4()), "session_id": session_id})


def mcp_call(method, params, req_id):
    """One MCP request. Like the real CLI it accepts a JSON body or an event stream (a slow call): comments and
    notifications/progress are skipped, the message with our id is the answer. The 10 s socket timeout applies to the
    first byte and to every pause between two lines, like a client's first-byte and idle budgets."""
    with open(mcp_config) as f:
        cfg = json.load(f)
    server = list(cfg["mcpServers"].values())[0]
    if method == "tools/call":
        params = dict(params, _meta={"progressToken": "fake-%d" % req_id})
    body = json.dumps({"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": req_id, "method": method, "params": params}).encode()
    headers = {"Content-Type": "application/json", "Accept": "application/json, text/event-stream"}
    headers.update(server.get("headers", {}))
    req = urllib.request.Request(server["url"], data=body, headers=headers, method="POST")
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10) as resp:
        if not resp.headers.get("Content-Type", "").startswith("text/event-stream"):
            return json.loads(resp.read().decode())
        data = []
        while True:
            line = resp.readline()
            if not line:
                raise RuntimeError("event stream ended without an answer")
            line = line.decode().rstrip("\r\n")
            if line.startswith("data:"):
                data.append(line[5:].lstrip())
            elif line == "" and data:
                msg = json.loads("\n".join(data))
                data = []
                if msg.get("id") == req_id:
                    return msg


def mcp_tool_roundtrip(tool, arguments, req_id):
    """Calls a factory MCP tool and shows it in the transcript like the real CLI does. Returns (text, is_error)."""
    tid = "toolu_fake_" + uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]
    emit({"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": msg_id(), "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "model": model,
                                           "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": tid, "name": "mcp__factory__" + tool, "input": arguments}]},
          "parent_tool_use_id": None, "session_id": session_id, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
    try:
        res = mcp_call("tools/call", {"name": tool, "arguments": arguments}, req_id)
        text = res["result"]["content"][0]["text"]
        is_error = bool(res["result"].get("isError"))
    except Exception as e:  # noqa
        text, is_error = "MCP call failed: %s" % e, True
    emit({"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": tid, "type": "tool_result", "content": text, "is_error": is_error}]},
          "parent_tool_use_id": None, "session_id": session_id, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
    return text, is_error


def tiny_png(width=4, height=3, rgb=(0x2B, 0x6C, 0xB0)):
    """A valid, uncompressed-colour PNG of one solid colour (no dependencies)."""
    def chunk(kind, data):
        return struct.pack(">I", len(data)) + kind + data + struct.pack(">I", zlib.crc32(kind + data) & 0xFFFFFFFF)
    raw = b"".join(b"\x00" + bytes(rgb) * width for _ in range(height))
    return (b"\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n" + chunk(b"IHDR", struct.pack(">IIBBBBB", width, height, 8, 2, 0, 0, 0)) +
            chunk(b"IDAT", zlib.compress(raw)) + chunk(b"IEND", b""))


def attach_fake_screenshot(prompt):
    """fake:screenshots: one screenshot through factory_attach_screenshot; returns the line for the summary."""
    m = re.search(r"after fix round (\d+)", prompt)
    when = "fix round %s" % m.group(1) if m else "build"
    name = "agern-fake-screenshot-%s.png" % role
    try:
        with open(name, "wb") as f:
            f.write(tiny_png())
        mcp_call("initialize", {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "fake-claude", "version": "0"}}, 1)
        text, is_error = mcp_tool_roundtrip("factory_attach_screenshot",
                                            {"path": name, "caption": "Fake %s screenshot (%s)" % (role, when)}, 2)
    except Exception as e:  # noqa
        text, is_error = "Screenshot failed: %s" % e, True
    finally:
        try:
            os.remove(name)
        except OSError:
            pass
    return text if is_error else "Attached 1 screenshot."


def mcp_init():
    mcp_call("initialize", {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "fake-claude", "version": "0"}}, 1)


def generate_fake_image(text, req_id=2):
    """fake:image[=<n>] [#<issue>]: calls factory_generate_image with purpose "app icon". Returns (answer, is_error)."""
    m = re.search(r"fake:image=(\d+)", text)
    args = {"prompt": "A friendly squirrel app icon, flat style (fake prompt)", "purpose": "app icon", "size": "256x256"}
    if m:
        args["count"] = int(m.group(1))
    issue = re.search(r"#(\d+)", text)
    if issue and role == "chat":
        args["issueNumber"] = int(issue.group(1))
    try:
        mcp_init()
        return mcp_tool_roundtrip("factory_generate_image", args, req_id)
    except Exception as e:  # noqa
        return "Image tool failed: %s" % e, True


def prepared_report(prompt):
    """The <images> block of a task prompt: one line per listed path, whether the file is there."""
    block = re.search(r"<images>(.*?)</images>", prompt, re.S)
    if not block:
        return ""
    lines = []
    for path in re.findall(r"^\s*path: (\S+)\s*$", block.group(1), re.M):
        if os.path.isfile(path):
            lines.append("PREPARED ok %s %d" % (path, os.path.getsize(path)))
        else:
            lines.append("PREPARED missing %s" % path)
    return "".join("\n" + l for l in lines)


def image_size(data):
    """(width, height) of PNG/GIF/JPEG bytes, or None."""
    import struct
    if data[:8] == b"\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n":
        return struct.unpack(">II", data[16:24])
    if data[:4] == b"GIF8":
        return struct.unpack("<HH", data[6:10])
    if data[:3] == b"\xff\xd8\xff":
        i = 2
        while i + 9 < len(data):
            if data[i] != 0xFF:
                i += 1
                continue
            mk = data[i + 1]
            if 0xC0 <= mk <= 0xCF and mk not in (0xC4, 0xC8, 0xCC):
                h, w = struct.unpack(">HH", data[i + 5:i + 9])
                return w, h
            if mk in (0xD8, 0x01) or 0xD0 <= mk <= 0xD7 or mk == 0xFF:
                i += 2 if mk != 0xFF else 1
                continue
            i += 2 + struct.unpack(">H", data[i + 2:i + 4])[0]
    return None


def describe_blocks(blocks):
    """What an attachment-carrying user turn contained, so tests can see the agent really got it."""
    import base64
    import re
    out = []
    n = 0
    for b in blocks:
        if not isinstance(b, dict):
            continue
        if b.get("type") == "image":
            n += 1
            src = b.get("source", {})
            try:
                data = base64.b64decode(src.get("data", ""), validate=True)
                size = image_size(data)
                dims = "%dx%d" % size if size else "?x?"
                out.append("IMAGE %d: %s %s, %d bytes" % (n, src.get("media_type"), dims, len(data)))
            except Exception as e:  # noqa
                out.append("IMAGE %d: undecodable (%s)" % (n, e))
        elif b.get("type") == "text" and b.get("text", "").startswith("[Attachments]"):
            lines = b["text"].splitlines()
            for i, line in enumerate(lines):
                m = re.match(r"\s+path: (.+)$", line)
                if not m:
                    continue
                path = m.group(1)
                head = re.match(r"\d+\. (.+?) — ", lines[i - 1]) if i > 0 else None
                name = head.group(1) if head else os.path.basename(path)
                if os.path.isfile(path):
                    inside_repo = os.path.abspath(path).startswith(os.getcwd() + os.sep)
                    out.append("FILE ok %s %d bytes%s" % (name, os.path.getsize(path), " (INSIDE THE REPO!)" if inside_repo else ""))
                else:
                    out.append("FILE missing %s at %s" % (name, path))
    return out


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- chat mode

advisor_context = {}


def advisor_reply(text, context):
    """The advisor's answer: the owner's words, what the run context says, and the actual diff."""
    lines = ["Advisor: " + text]
    for line in context.splitlines():
        if line.startswith("Needs a human because:") or line.startswith("### "):
            lines.append(line)
    base = re.search(r"git diff (\S+)\.\.\.HEAD", context)
    if "please change" in text and (os.path.isdir(".git") or os.path.isfile(".git")):
        with open("AGERN_FAKE.md", "a") as f:
            f.write("change requested in the conversation at %s\n" % time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S"))
        subprocess.run(["git", "add", "AGERN_FAKE.md"], check=False)
        subprocess.run(["git", "commit", "-q", "-m", "Apply the change the run owner asked for (fake)"], check=False)
        lines.append("Committed the change; the factory pushes it and has it reviewed again. Only you can approve the run.")
    if base:
        ref = base.group(1).strip("`")
        try:
            stat = subprocess.run(["git", "diff", "--stat", "%s...HEAD" % ref], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30).stdout.strip()
        except Exception as e:  # noqa
            stat = "git diff failed: %s" % e
        lines.append("Diff: " + (stat or "(no changes)"))
    return "\n".join(lines)


def chat_mode():
    inbox = queue.Queue()

    def reader():
        for line in sys.stdin:
            line = line.strip()
            if line:
                try:
                    inbox.put(json.loads(line))
                except ValueError:
                    pass
        inbox.put(None)

    threading.Thread(target=reader, daemon=True).start()
    pending = []
    interrupt_flag = {"set": False}

    def drain_controls():
        while True:
            try:
                m = inbox.get_nowait()
            except queue.Empty:
                return
            if m is None:
                pending.append(None)
            elif m.get("type") == "control_request":
                handle_control(m)
            else:
                pending.append(m)

    def handle_control(m):
        if m.get("request", {}).get("subtype") == "interrupt":
            interrupt_flag["set"] = True
        emit({"type": "control_response", "response": {"subtype": "success", "request_id": m.get("request_id"), "response": {}}})

    while True:
        if pending:
            m = pending.pop(0)
        else:
            m = inbox.get()
        if m is None:
            return
        if m.get("type") == "control_request":
            handle_control(m)
            continue
        if m.get("type") != "user":
            continue
        content = m.get("message", {}).get("content", "")
        attachment_report = []
        if isinstance(content, list):
            attachment_report = describe_blocks(content)
            content = " ".join(c.get("text", "") for c in content
                               if isinstance(c, dict) and c.get("type") == "text" and not c.get("text", "").startswith("[Attachments]"))
        interrupt_flag["set"] = False
        init_event()
        forward = re.match(r"\s*forward (\S+) (\S+?):\s*(.+)$", content, re.S)
        if forward and mcp_config:
            try:
                mcp_call("initialize", {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "fake-claude", "version": "0"}}, 1)
                res = mcp_call("tools/call", {"name": "factory_send_to_agent", "arguments": {
                    "runId": forward.group(1), "role": forward.group(2), "message": forward.group(3).strip()}}, 2)
                text = res["result"]["content"][0]["text"]
                reply = ("Could not forward it: " if res["result"].get("isError") else "Forwarded. ") + text
            except Exception as e:  # noqa
                reply = "MCP call failed: %s" % e
            stream_text(reply)
            result(reply)
            continue
        file_issue = re.match(r"\s*file issue:\s*(.+)$", content, re.S)
        if file_issue and mcp_config:
            try:
                mcp_call("initialize", {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "fake-claude", "version": "0"}}, 1)
                res = mcp_call("tools/call", {"name": "factory_create_issue", "arguments": {
                    "title": file_issue.group(1).strip(), "body": "Filed by fake-claude", "kind": "bug"}}, 2)
                text = res["result"]["content"][0]["text"]
                reply = ("Could not file it: " if res["result"].get("isError") else "") + text
            except Exception as e:  # noqa
                reply = "MCP call failed: %s" % e
            stream_text(reply)
            result(reply)
            continue
        if role == "advisor":
            context = advisor_context.get("text", "")
            m_ctx = re.search(r"<run_context>[\s\S]*?</run_context>", content)
            if m_ctx:
                context = m_ctx.group(0)
                advisor_context["text"] = context
            content = re.sub(r"<run_context>[\s\S]*?</run_context>\s*", "", content)
            content = owner_text(content.strip())
        if "crash" in content:
            sys.stderr.write("fake-claude: crashing as requested\n")
            sys.exit(3)
        if role == "advisor" and "slow" not in content:
            reply = advisor_reply(content, advisor_context.get("text", ""))
            stream_text(reply)
            result(reply)
            continue
        rate_limit_event(content)
        if "fake:think" in content:
            think()
        if "fake:heartbeat" in content:
            heartbeat_tool()
        if "tool" in content:
            tool_roundtrip("echo hello from fake-claude && pwd")
        reply = "You said: " + content
        if attachment_report:
            reply += "\n" + "\n".join(attachment_report)
        if "long" in content:
            reply += "\n" + "\n".join("line %d of a long answer" % i for i in range(1, 81))
        if "env" in content:
            reply += "\nENV: " + ",".join(sorted(os.environ.keys()))
        if "mcp" in content and mcp_config:
            try:
                init = mcp_call("initialize", {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "fake-claude", "version": "0"}}, 1)
                tools = mcp_call("tools/list", {}, 2)
                names = [t["name"] for t in tools["result"]["tools"]]
                reply += "\nMCP server: %s\nTools: %s" % (init["result"]["serverInfo"]["name"], ", ".join(names))
            except Exception as e:  # noqa
                reply += "\nMCP call failed: %s" % e
        if "install" in content and mcp_config:
            try:
                mcp_call("initialize", {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "fake-claude", "version": "0"}}, 1)
                res = mcp_call("tools/call", {"name": "factory_request_software", "arguments": {
                    "name": "fake-toolchain", "reason": "fake-claude was asked to install something"}}, 2)
                reply += "\n" + res["result"]["content"][0]["text"]
            except Exception as e:  # noqa
                reply += "\nMCP call failed: %s" % e
        if "fake:image" in content and mcp_config:
            answer, _ = generate_fake_image(content)
            reply += "\nImage tool: " + answer
        if "slow" in content and not forward:
            chunks = ["%d " % i for i in range(1, 41)]
            ok, sent = stream_text("".join(chunks), chunk_delay=0.25, chunks=chunks,
                                   interrupted=lambda: (drain_controls() or interrupt_flag["set"]))
        else:
            ok, sent = stream_text(reply)
        if not ok:
            emit({"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[Request interrupted by user]"}]},
                  "parent_tool_use_id": None, "session_id": session_id, "uuid": str(uuid.uuid4())})
            result(None, subtype="error_during_execution", is_error=True, turns=1, cost=0.001)
        else:
            result(reply)


